WEBVTT

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.360
Is it a rabbit? Yeah, not likely...

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.730
I've never seen anything quite like it.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.100
Well, best to stay away from 
things you don't understand.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.390
I'll just leave it there.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.250
Fine, I get it! I get it!

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.720
Will a carrot do?

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.010
My name is Saltherine.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:33.560
Just call me Sally.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.510
I have a princess's order for you!

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.510
Well, technically, 
I'm not a princess anymore...

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.380
Do you speak human?

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.020
Some.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.070
I'm going to ask you a few questions.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:47.590
What's your name?

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:48.980
Frau!

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.520
Frau? Okay.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.530
Are you a monster, Frau?

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.250
Not monster. Harefolk.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:57.460
Harefolk?

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.010
<i>Ah... So this is a demihuman.</i>

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:05.730
<i>I'd heard there were non-human 
beings on the outside...</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.540
That's an interesting outfit you're wearing.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.290
Style!

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.240
Now, one last thing.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.490
Have you seen this person?

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:27.440
No.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:28.690
I see.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.410
Carrot was delicious!

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:34.440
S-Sure...

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.450
Delicious carrot. Thanks.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:39.950
Sure thing!

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:42.710
Well, Frau...

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.670
I've got to be going!

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.960
Take care of yourself this time, okay?

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:51.680
Follow!

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.960
Frau follows Sally!

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.050
Where did that come from?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.380
Carrot debt!

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.430
Honestly, it's no big deal!

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:08.480
The Ex-Princess and the Harefolk

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.520
<i>It really followed me...</i>

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.480
Don't you have somewhere else to be?

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:10.620
No!

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.980
That's no reason to follow <i>me</i>, though...

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.990
I wasn't trying to tame the strange thing...

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.490
Travel alone is dangerous!

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.830
Of course it is...

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:23.770
But travel with a demihuman 
might not be much better.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:26.200
Well, all right.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.000
You can stick with me as far as the village.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:39.830
Haven't seen you around!

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:41.090
Are you a traveler, by chance?

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:41.880
Yes.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.010
I see. Welcome to—

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.620
A demihuman!

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:55.310
I thought it might be conspicuous.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.400
Get out!

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.260
We can't let a demihuman into the village!

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:03.950
H-Hang on, now!

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.290
It may look weird, but it's 
not hostile or anything!

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.830
Don't let it deceive you, miss.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.040
Demihumans are our mortal enemies.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.750
Association with one is out of the question!

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.170
Now, come with me.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.490
We're leaving, Frau.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.570
No! Come with me!

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.990
Sally! Village is that way.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.490
Just come along.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:48.600
Princess's orders!

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:54.440
Okay.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.050
There's nobody at the entrance.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.730
Let's sneak inside quick!

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:00.840
Agreed.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:09.920
See? We made it!

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.900
And once we reach the inn—

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:12.570
Oh?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.920
Haven't seen you around.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.860
Are you a traveler, by chance?

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.120
Y-Yes.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.190
I just got here, actually!

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.600
I see.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:25.990
This may be a simple village...

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:28.740
but I hope you enjoy your stay.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.190
Carrots!

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.600
Wai— Frau!

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.630
Carrots!

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:34.920
Control yourself!

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.520
If you don't mind my saying,

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.780
you do appear hungry...

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:40.750
Hungry!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.630
You're welcome to stop by 
my mansion, if you wish.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.810
I'll treat you to dinner.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.460
You're the local lord, then?

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.300
Making travelers feel welcome 
is one of my duties.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.540
Anything I can provide, just say the word.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.280
Might I inquire as to your 
companion's whereabouts?

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:05.280
They were rather tired, I think...

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:08.960
They're resting in the room you prepared.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.400
That's a shame.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.730
I was hoping they'd join us for dinner.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.350
I'm so sorry!

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:19.190
Well, I only wish I could provide 
more than this peasant's feast.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.360
You must be tired from your journey.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:29.800
You can stay here as long as you like.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:31.910
You've done so much already.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.440
I don't know how to thank you.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:35.800
It's nothing, really.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:39.790
It wasn't until recently that we had 
the means to welcome travelers at all.

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:42.760
Our region became overrun by monsters.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.910
They killed many of my people.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.300
It was a deeply trying time.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.840
But one day, a young traveler happened by

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:01.090
who slew the monsters single-handedly.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.840
Did that traveler have long 
black hair, by chance?

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.340
Yes. A friend of yours, by chance?

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.710
<i>It's Mikoto! It has to be!</i>

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:15.220
Which way did the traveler go?

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:18.730
I wish I knew, but I'm afraid I don't.

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:21.200
I see.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.070
Regardless...

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:28.580
In our gratitude for that 
traveler's generous act,

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:31.070
I think we'll welcome all 
travelers from now on.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.120
Get out!

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.600
We can't let a demihuman into the village!

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.310
Demihumans...

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.870
You don't welcome demihumans, do you?

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.980
Even if they're travelers...

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:55.120
No village could ever welcome demihumans.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:07:00.990
But it's an intriguing idea... 
a demihuman traveler!

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:01.870
Why not?

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:05.750
I see...

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:09.360
Perhaps you're too young to know.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:14.160
Demihumans are savage and stupid by birth.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.660
They're as bad as monsters, 
from a human perspective.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:22.040
Put simply, demihumans 
are our mortal enemies.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:29.550
<i>Frau doesn't seem so bad to me...</i>

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.290
<i>Forget it.</i>

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.830
I said we'd stick together 
as far as the village.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.270
So when it's time to leave,

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.420
I'll just...

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:55.570
A monster!

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.280
There's a monster in town!

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.080
A monster?!

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.140
Was there a survivor?

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:02.420
It can't be!

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:03.580
Look! It's got horns!

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:05.430
That's no ordinary monster!

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.170
That's an ogre!

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:10.930
But it's alone, see?

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.410
I'm sure someone can handle it...

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:13.880
Are you stupid or something?

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:16.240
<i>That's not a monster!</i>

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:18.360
<i>An ogre?</i>

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:28.010
<i>That feeling... It's happening again.</i>

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.490
<i>Just like before...</i>

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.540
<i>I feel...</i>

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:35.050
<i>hot all over!</i>

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.240
Stop it! Get back!

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:45.360
What the...

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:49.810
Why am I...

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:53.070
I'm going to... die?

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.460
Thanks so much, Frau!

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.210
A demihuman!

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.050
It slew a monster barehanded...

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:25.870
It's terrifying!

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.280
Hang on, now...

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:31.090
Frau just saved this village!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.380
But just because they're a demihuman...

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:36.420
The savagery sufficient to slay an ogre...

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:39.070
Our fear of demihumans 
is thoroughly justified!

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.180
Your Lordship...

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:46.140
Leave our village at once!

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:47.900
Frau?

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:51.940
You're...

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.890
Carrots were tasty.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.030
Thanks.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.910
Princess's orders. We're leaving, Frau.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.070
Agreed!

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:11.820
Your Lordship! Are you just going 
to let the demihuman escape?

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.920
It could come back and attack at any minute!

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:19.560
It said... thank you.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:21.160
Your Lordship?

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:28.040
I hope you changed a few minds back there.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:29.870
Hold it, you two!

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.720
I'm with the Knights of Rimdarl.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:36.940
I have a few questions for you!

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:46.530
m 0 0 l 0 50 l 150 50 l 150 0

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:46.530
<b>Northern Empire
Kingdom of Rimdarl</b>

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:57.570
How'd we end up in this mess?

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:58.800
Sorry about that.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:02.440
I thought the cell and the 
shackles were a bit much...

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:04.560
But you're hanging with a demihuman, y'know?

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.590
More demihuman hate...

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.460
Sorry for all the unpleasantries.

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:16.070
Come on out, now.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.060
So you're...

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:25.380
Hawthorn Grattor,

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.450
regimental commander of the royal knights.

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.170
I'm Sally.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:32.140
That there's Frau.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:34.400
Still sore, are you?

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:35.710
You bet I am!

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:40.220
As if being a demihuman—or traveling with 
one—is any excuse for this treatment...

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:43.220
Is that the only reason you arrested us?

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.000
Not quite.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.250
It's because it's a demihuman savage enough

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:53.440
to slay an ogre barehanded.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.230
You saw that?

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:58.670
I was on the road.

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:02.240
But a demihuman capable of fighting—

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:04.600
rather, of easily slaying an ogre—

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:06.610
was the last thing I expected to see.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.820
Everyone sees demihumans as monsters.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:13.570
You're not wrong about that.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.500
I used to be the same way.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:16.880
Used to?

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:20.270
I told you, I saw it.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:24.390
I saw that thing fight to protect you,

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.690
and then bow in respect 
to the local big shot.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:34.340
Fighting to protect another is 
a sign of a chivalrous heart.

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:36.310
Am I right, demihuman?

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:38.070
Or rather... Frau?

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.090
Now, let's get you out of here.

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.540
What? Already?

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.540
As easy as that?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.160
Easy as that.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:59.070
It was an unjust arrest 
of two innocent travelers.

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:00.760
The fault's entirely ours.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:02.730
Hawthorn!

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:05.570
I'll take the heat if the hammer comes down.

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:07.340
You two rest easy.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.060
Hungry.

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:17.490
Relief gets the appetite raging, huh?

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.020
I hear you, Frau!

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.570
We've certainly been put through 
the wringer, haven't we?

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.740
The unjust arrest of two 
good-hearted, innocent travelers,

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:33.060
who are on the verge of starvation after
a brutal interrogation with no food or water!

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:35.330
Where'd you get this little improv routine?

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:37.490
You force us

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:42.880
to demand food-related restitution!

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.940
H-Hang on!

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:48.920
You can't start making demands 
the minute you're safe!

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:54.810
Lunch only, you hear me?

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.730
Don't try fishing for a free dinner.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:58.190
How come?

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.050
Give me a dang break.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:04.740
You think us knights make 
feed-other-people-multiple-times kind of money?

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:06.740
Come back and see us, Master Hawthorn!

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:11.740
We just got a fresh catch in!

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:20.990
Sally?

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:22.630
I'll pass.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.190
I'm not alone today.

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:25.720
It's Hawthorn!

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:31.490
What're you doing here?

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.250
Is this your sweetheart?

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.520
Awesome!

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.490
Check out the knockers on her!

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:39.590
No way!

00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:41.890
He's not my type one bit!

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:42.440
Hey.

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:43.770
Carrots!

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:47.920
Welcome!

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.300
Mr. Hawthorn, if you please?

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.740
Yeah, yeah. It's all on my tab, right?

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:00.610
An unsightly castle, don't you agree?

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:06.300
A mere hut. I could topple it all by myself.

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:12.290
m 0 0 l 0 64 l 140 64 l 140 0

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:12.290
<b>High Ogre of the East

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:11.130
Don't forget, Sett, that it was 
the Kishin who paired us up.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:17.300
<b>Walrus Ogre of the North

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:17.310
m 0 0 l 0 64 l 140 64 l 140 0

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:14.560
Don't remind me.

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:16.640
Let's just get this done.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.430
Indeed.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.280
Let us make quick work of it!

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:33.910
Wait up!

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:45.750
What's that sound?

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:11.600
Look at you, Meki! You look ridiculous!

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.740
The use of my cannon causes me to shrink!

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:17.060
I'll recover soon enough.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:18.740
Proceed without me!

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:20.650
Yeah, I hear you.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:25.290
Halt!

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.670
You're no mere monster, are you?

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.260
I see that horn! You're an ogre!

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.840
We do not abide the ingress of ogres to—

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:53.230
Don't waste time prattling with an 
enemy in your midst, foolish humans!

00:17:01.510 --> 00:17:02.400
<i>Ogre.</i>

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:09.080
Sally!

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:10.050
Hey, Sally!

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:11.720
What are you doing?

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:12.840
You have to go!

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:14.870
Sally!

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:16.050
Can't she hear me?

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:18.080
Human.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.940
There's defiance in your eyes.

00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:22.320
Damn it!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:33.460
A demihuman? How surprising!

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.250
That kick didn't even dent it!

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:38.700
Sally!

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.930
What? What am I...

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:44.490
You're back with us at last!

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.210
Sally!

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.210
Run fast!

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.360
Run far!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.480
I can't just leave you!

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:54.090
Come on! We can't stay!

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.320
Hey! Hawthorn!

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:00.050
A demihuman in a human settlement...

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:02.100
That's surprising enough on its own.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.810
But one this determined to assist them...

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.730
It's unprecedented!

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.010
Carrot debt.

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:13.180
Sally was not afraid of Frau.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.110
Frau wants to remain with Sally.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:18.050
So Frau protects Sally.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.110
The end!

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:24.270
And that's enough to spur 
you to take me on, eh?

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:27.080
I like your spirit!

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:30.550
My name is Sett!

00:18:30.550 --> 00:18:31.880
Speak your name, harefolk!

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:34.800
Frau!

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.480
Get the citizens to safety!

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:38.380
Hurry!

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:41.790
Captain, the monster's still out there!

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:43.120
I know.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.950
But evacuations come first.

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:47.460
We can slay the monster when that's done.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:48.040
Sir!

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.100
Where'd Sally go?

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:01.540
Good attack.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:03.870
But I didn't even feel it!

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:07.510
You've got speed, but you lack impact...

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.130
You hop around too willy-nilly.

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:19.960
I've got you now!

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.640
This 'fight' is over.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:27.360
I'm impressed. You're still defiant.

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:29.140
I almost hate to kill you!

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:30.540
How about this?

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:33.260
Abandon those humans and head for the hills.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.780
I'll let you live.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:41.660
Frau protects Sally.

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:44.260
No running.

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.770
I respect that.

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:49.660
In that case...

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.680
As a show of my respect,

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:00.170
I'll kill you with all I have!

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:06.180
Sally...

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.600
Goodbye.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.810
Don't give up, stupid!

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.320
Farewell to you, harefolk warrior!

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:33.350
How impressive...

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:36.300
A suicide attack from that position.

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:38.340
I did feel that one, lightly.

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.260
But you're through now.

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:44.930
Frau!

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:47.850
I know you!

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:51.490
You're the human the 
harefolk wanted to protect.

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:54.220
What excellent timing!

00:20:54.220 --> 00:20:56.780
I can send you to the grave together!

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.400
Sally. Run... fast.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:04.210
Sally?

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:06.910
<i>This feeling again.</i>

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:09.660
<i>I feel hot all over.</i>

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:13.060
<i>But I also...</i>

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.300
<i>Once upon a time, in a far away land,</i>

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:21.090
<i>lived an old man and an old lady.</i>

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:23.610
Harefolk warrior Frau!

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:24.670
<i>The old man went to the mountains 
to gather firewood.</i>

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:26.580
Human of appellation unknown!

00:21:25.270 --> 00:21:27.690
<i>The old woman went to the 
river to do the washing.</i>

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:29.100
<i>You know the story.</i>

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:31.270
Farewell!

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:36.140
<i>At last, he'd defeated the ogre,</i>

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:39.140
<i>but upon hearing there 
were ogres in other lands,</i>

00:21:40.890 --> 00:21:43.610
<i>Peach Boy set out to cross the great sea...</i>

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:48.570
Wh-What?!

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:50.620
<i>Now, here's a what-if for you to ponder...</i>

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:52.450
What in the world?!

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:54.570
<i>What if more than one peach</i>

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:57.540
<i>came down the river?</i>

00:21:57.540 --> 00:22:00.140
<i>...feel so good.</i>

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:06.770
<i>What if that peach,</i>

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.530
<i>which came down the river,</i>

00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:12.580
<i>was just one of many?</i>

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:49.990
Ogres and Humans

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:49.490
Next time: "Ogres and Humans."
